fact WorkItem(id: "WI-088", description: some(value: "Marshalling as an extension of TypeMapping (not a separate mechanism). SUPERSEDES the original Vec3FromConstDoublePtr3 marker family (too partial: each marker baked target-type x source-rep x arity into its NAME and needed one hardcoded Rust handler in cpp-gen — a closed enumeration recompiled per combo; and was inbound-only by construction — \"From\" only lifts host->anthill, so every input-position vector would have forced a mirror Vec3ToDoublePtr3 marker, doubling the partiality). Also REPLACES the return-only ReturnTypeConversion fact currently in cpp_std (return-only by construction; repeats per-operation — 5 near-identical facts in lf1). KEY INSIGHT: a coercion is just a TypeMapping entry whose value-level conversion is not identity — so collapse the two into ONE concept. Extend TypeMapping with an optional lift/lower adapter pair: an entry with NO adapter is a plain rename (Int -> int64_t, identity at the value level, today's behaviour); an entry WITH an adapter is marshalled (Vec3 -> `const double *`, via from_array (lift) and to_array/fill (lower)). This dissolves the former open question (how does codegen know a carrier method's foreign signature, since the spec abstracts it to Vec3): the host signature is DERIVED, not annotated and not separately recorded — codegen computes the carrier method's foreign signature by mapping the operation's declared anthill types through the type map (host_sig(get_values) = typemap(Vec3) = `const double *`). Where the foreign rep differs from the anthill slot's default rep and the entry carries an adapter, codegen bridges. Inherently bidirectional: the same entry's LOWER fires for a Vec3 passed INTO a host-API call (generated controllers CALL the API, so input args must be transformed to the foreign rep before the call), its LIFT for a value read back. SCOPE (load-bearing, non-obvious): Vec3 has TWO host reps — its generated struct anthill::...::types::Vec3{x,y,z} in anthill-land (the `position: Vec3` field, desired_position(offset: Vec3) -> Vec3, constructed facts) and `const double *` at the webots carrier boundary. So adapter-bearing entries MUST NOT be global in cpp_std (that would lower every Vec3 everywhere to `const double *` and break the struct, pure ops, and fields). They live in the FOREIGN BINDING — the webots realization, alongside the CarrierBindings that already map GPS -> webots::GPS* — scoped to that API surface; plain renames stay global in cpp_std (WI-089). The coercion fires exactly at the boundary where a binding-mapped value meets a default-mapped slot, which is the carrier-method call site codegen already identifies (synthesise_body_for paths 2/3). Covers GPS.get_values / get_speed_vector, Gyro.get_values, Receiver.get_emitter_direction (lift today) plus any future setter / Supervisor-field write taking a vector (lower); variants (EulerAngles, Vec4) are one type-map entry + one hand-authored adapter pair each, never a cpp-gen recompile. Lives in webots/marshalling.anthill (or the webots realization) project-local until a second consumer needs it; then lift the shape (not the entries) to cpp_std."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-089"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-27T17:36:12Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-088", author: "user", content: "REOPENED: the reader is built on an ad-hoc mechanism and must use the standard one. MarshalTable::from_kb scans free-floating top-level TypeMapping facts via kb.rules_by_functor(TypeMapping), keyed only by anthill_type in a flat map with NO profile and NO binding scope — a parallel reading path running alongside the (still-unbuilt) standard LanguageMapping reader. The data model is right (TypeMapping with optional lift/lower); the READER is wrong. Correction: there is ONE type-mapping reader (the LanguageMapping reader WI-089 establishes); renames and marshalled entries flow through it identically; the rename-vs-marshalled distinction is adapter-presence WITHIN a single map — exactly WI-088 own thesis (a coercion is just a TypeMapping entry whose value-level conversion is not identity / collapse into ONE concept), which the implementation then re-split at the reading layer. The only force that pushed marshalling to a free-floating fact was SCOPE (a global Vec3->const double* would lower the struct/pure-ops/fields). The correct answer to scope is a SCOPED language mapping, not a loose fact: the profile LanguageMapping (cpp_std) is the global base; the foreign binding (webots realization) owns an OVERLAY carrying the adapter-bearing entries. The standard reader composes base+overlay; boundary-only application stays at the dispatch site (synthesise_body_for); declared-signature lowering (sort_to_cpp) reads the same map but ignores adapters. Retire MarshalTable into the WI-089 standard reader and migrate the entries from free-floating facts into the binding scoped LanguageMapping. Bonus: the current global rules_by_functor scan has a latent collision (two bindings mapping the same type differently, last-wins) that a scope-aware reader fixes.", at: "2026-06-25T12:44:10Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-088", author: "user", content: "APPROACH UPDATE (supersedes the scope-aware-reader wording in the prior feedback): WI-089 makes type-mapping an ORDINARY KB QUERY over KEYED entries (keys, NOT tags) and retires MarshalTable with NO replacement reader. So the WI-088 migration is: give the webots Vec3/EulerAngles TypeMapping entries a key (webots, reused from NamespaceMapping.host_module) so the standard lower_type query picks them up at carrier boundaries; delete MarshalTable. No bespoke marshalling reader survives.", at: "2026-06-25T12:44:20Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-088", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED via WI-089 increment (a) (commit 19b53dc1, merged to main 31d58bbf). The marshalling = keyed-TypeMapping design landed exactly as specced: TypeMapping carries optional lift/lower; adapter-bearing entries are scoped to the FOREIGN BINDING (webots), keyed key:some(webots) + lang:some(cpp), selected ONLY at the carrier-dispatch boundary via the active-key list [binding?,profile?,none] so Vec3 stays its generated struct in fields/pure-ops/signatures and becomes const double* only at the webots boundary. Host signature DERIVED (marshal_for_type maps declared anthill types through the query); lift fires on returns (Vec3::from_array), lower on args (Vec3::to_array). MarshalTable retired (one reader: the same keyed TypeMapping query as renames). Vec3FromConstDoublePtr marker family + return-only ReturnTypeConversion superseded/removed. Covers GPS/Gyro/InertialUnit/Receiver getters (Vec3 + EulerAngles). Tests: conversion_test (5) + lf1 GPS traits, cpp-gen 119/0. The binding key is an explicit Implementation.binding field (the design note saying reuse NamespaceMapping.host_module was superseded by the WI-089(a) explicit-binding decision).", at: "2026-06-27T17:36:16Z")
